D = {
"Fire-Wrapped Golden Fish|HFFOTM": "Heat oil to 360°F and the oven to 200°F. Season the fish. Chill a flour and spice mix over ice water, then stir in sparkling water for a lumpy batter. Fry battered fish in two rounds of three pieces for 4 to 5 minutes, turning, holding 360°F. Drain, salt, and keep warm in the oven. Serve with lime wedges.",
"Flash-Fried Berry Fritters|HFLOTT": "Heat 4 inches of oil to 360°F. Mix a batter of flour, baking powder, cinnamon, salt, egg, sugar, milk, vanilla, and butter, then fold in flour-dusted blueberries. Drop 2-tablespoon portions into the oil and fry about 3 minutes, turning once, until deep golden. Drain, dust with confectioners' sugar, and serve warm or at room temperature.",
"Flumphcakes|PAF": "Mix the dry ingredients. Whisk buttermilk, sugar, egg yolk, and melted butter, then combine with the dry mix, leaving some lumps. Fold in a softly whipped egg white and rest 15 minutes. Cook 1½ tablespoon dollops in butter over medium heat, 1 to 2 minutes until bubbly, then flip and cook 2 more minutes until golden. Drain on paper towels.",
"Fol-De-Rol|PAF": "Muddle cherries in a shaker, then add vodka, maraschino liqueur, coconut water, and lime juice. Add ice and shake about 30 seconds. Put a Luxardo cherry in each of two glasses, strain the drink over them, and serve at once.",
"Fried Bread and Spices|HFFOTM": "Mix paprika, cumin, coriander, fennel, salt, pepper, and cayenne. Oil both sides of each bread slice and cook in a skillet over medium heat for about 5 minutes until golden underneath. Sprinkle spices on top near the end. Flip and cook about 1½ minutes more. Rub with garlic if you like.",
"Fried Fingers|HF": "Simmer a sauce of scallion, ginger, garlic, five-spice, jam, vinegar, soy sauce, and brown sugar for 4 to 6 minutes. Toast panko at 325°F for 8 to 10 minutes and season it with crushed chips. Dredge chicken strips in flour, egg, then panko. Bake at 500°F for 10 to 12 minutes, turning midway. Cool 4 minutes and serve with the sauce.",
"Fried Soy with Vegetables|HFFOTM": "Press sliced tofu for 20 minutes, then marinate in soy sauce, rice wine, and sesame oil for 15 minutes. Brown the tofu 2½ to 3½ minutes per side on high heat. Sear bok choy about 2 minutes per side, then cook carrots and pepper about 2 minutes. Fry ginger and garlic 45 seconds, add the sauce 45 seconds, then toss everything together for 1 minute.",
"Fruit and Ricotta Pancakes|HFLOTT": "Whisk mascarpone, honey, and walnut oil for a topping. Preheat the oven to 200°F. Mix yolks, sugar, orange zest, ricotta, buttermilk, vanilla, butter, then sifted dry ingredients. Fold in stiff beaten whites. Cook batter rounds with fig pieces on medium-low heat, about 1½ minutes, flip, and cook 2½ minutes more. Keep warm, then top with the mascarpone and walnuts.",
"Gaeth'ad|HFLOTT": "Chill a pitcher of green tea sweetened with elderflower syrup. Fan sliced strawberries on picks. Press a cucumber ribbon against the inside of each of two glasses, fill halfway with ice, and pour in the tea. Add a strawberry, an apple slice, and an orange slice. Garnish with slapped mint and the strawberry picks, then serve immediately.",
"Gingerbread Man|HF": "Process flour, spices, melted butter, molasses, milk, and vanilla into dough for 15 to 30 seconds. Chill two disks at least 1 hour. Roll ¼ inch thick, cut with a 3½-inch cutter, and bake at 350°F for 9 to 11 minutes, rotating midway. Cool 10 minutes, then decorate with whipped icing, currants, and walnuts. Dry 45 minutes. Keeps 2 days.",
"Gnomish Garlic Chicken|HFLOTT": "Cook garlic in oil on low for 20 to 25 minutes, then set it aside. Brown chicken skin-side down for about 8 minutes. Build a sauce from flour, thyme, sherry, broth, water, and bay leaves. Return chicken with half the garlic and bake at 325°F for 25 to 30 minutes until 195°F. Mash the garlic into the sauce with lemon juice and parsley.",
"Golden Melon Salad with Lemony Yogurt and Chiles|HFLOTT": "Whisk yogurt, honey, shallot, lemon zest and juice, coriander, salt, and pepper into a dressing. Peel and seed a cantaloupe, cut it into ½-inch slices, and halve them. Arrange on a platter, drizzle with the dressing, sprinkle with mint and chile, and serve immediately.",
"Golden Way|PAF": "Muddle cantaloupe in a shaker until the juices come out. Add sake, orange liqueur, yuzu juice, and honey, plus ice. Shake 30 seconds. Strain evenly into two coupe glasses and serve at once.",
"Goldenstars|HFFOTM": "Knead a dough of flour, sugar, onion powder, baking powder, eggs, oil, and water. Rest 1 hour. Cook a filling of sausage, potato, leek, thyme, flour, and broth, then cool 10 to 15 minutes. Cut 4-inch rounds, fill, fold into triangles, and seal. Brush with egg wash and bake at 375°F for about 25 minutes, rotating. Cool 5 minutes.",
"Goodberry Blend|HF": "Crush ice in a blender. Add orange juice, spinach, honey, and salt and blend 20 to 60 seconds until liquid. Add blueberries and banana and blend about 45 seconds until thick and smooth. Pour into four cups and serve immediately.",
"Green Dragon Blackbread Muffins|HFFOTM": "Preheat the oven to 400°F. Whisk the flours, cornmeal, cocoa, baking soda, salt, and baking powder. Whisk oil, butter, molasses, brown sugar, egg, and buttermilk, then fold into the dry mix without overmixing. Add currants if wanted. Fill 12 cups and bake about 15 minutes, rotating. Cool 12 minutes in the tin. Serve with soft butter.",
"Green Ice Rime|HFFOTM": "Soften gelatin in 1½ cups milk for 10 minutes. Warm the other 3 cups milk with sugar and salt for about 7 minutes. Whisk in the gelatin and cool 10 minutes. Add mint extract, vanilla, and food coloring. Pour into an oiled 8 or 9-inch pan and chill about 4 hours, up to 2 days. Cut into 2-inch squares and serve in chilled goblets.",
"Green Onion Pancakes|HFFOTM": "Warm the oven to 250°F. Chill a crème fraîche and milk dip. Whisk a loose batter from flour, onion powder, baking powder, egg, water, soy sauce, and oil. Add cabbage, carrot, and scallions and rest 5 minutes. Cook each 7-inch pancake in a skillet about 3½ minutes per side. Keep warm. Cool 4 minutes, cut into wedges, and serve with the dip.",
"Greengrass|PAF": "In each of two highball glasses, muddle half the cilantro and limes with 2 teaspoons sugar. Fill three-quarters with ice. Divide cachaca and falernum between the glasses. Top with soda water, stir gently, and serve at once.",
"Greenspear Bundles in Bacon|HF": "Preheat the oven to 425°F. Toss asparagus with olive oil, salt, and pepper. Wrap four spears in each bacon slice to make eight bundles. Arrange seam-side down on a rimmed baking sheet, 1 inch apart. Roast about 15 minutes until the bacon and asparagus are cooked and browned. Sprinkle with chives and serve at once.",
"Gully Dwarf Homestyle Porridge|HF": "Melt butter on medium heat and toast oats about 4 minutes. Add water and simmer on medium-high, stirring. Add milk and simmer gently on medium-low for 10 to 15 minutes until thick and tender. Stir in salt and 3 tablespoons brown sugar. Cover and rest 5 minutes. Top each serving with 1½ teaspoons cream and 1 teaspoon brown sugar.",
"Gurdats|HF": "Preheat the oven to 425°F. Toss mushroom caps in oil, lemon juice, and salt. Roast gill-side up 15 to 18 minutes, drain, flip, and roast 6 to 10 minutes more. Cook chopped stems with shallot, thyme, garlic, and sherry, then mix with breadcrumbs, parsley, Peppadews, Parmesan, and cream cheese. Fill the caps, crumb the tops, and roast 15 to 20 minutes.",
"Halfling Game Birds|HFFOTM": "Spatchcock two Cornish hens, halve them, and rub lemon, rosemary, thyme, and salt under the skin. Chill uncovered 4 to 24 hours. Heat the oven to 500°F with a baking sheet inside. Roast the hens skin-side down for 10 minutes. Flip and broil 6 to 9 minutes until 160°F in the breast and 175°F in the thigh. Serve immediately.",
"Halfling Iron Rations|HFFOTM": "Preheat the oven to 325°F. Mix oats, almonds, walnuts, pepitas, flaxseed, and sesame seeds. Coat with a whisked blend of egg white, olive oil, Worcestershire, brown sugar, and spices. Press ⅜ inch thick on a lined sheet. Bake about 25 minutes, turn, and bake 5 more. Cool to crisp. Keeps 2 weeks airtight.",
"Halfling Oatmeal Sweet Nibbles|HF": "Preheat the oven to 350°F. Combine flour, oats, baking soda, and salt. Cream brown sugar and butter, then mix in egg, vanilla, the dry mix, and chocolate and butterscotch chips. Scoop rounded tablespoons 2 inches apart. Bake 15 minutes, rotating midway, in two batches. Cool on the sheet, then on a rack. Keeps 3 days.",
"Hand Of Vecna|PAF": "Rinse two rocks glasses with ¼ ounce absinthe each, then discard the excess. Muddle sugar into Angostura bitters to a syrup in a mixing glass. Add scotch and ice and stir about 30 seconds. Put large ice cubes in the glasses, strain the drink evenly into them, garnish with orange peel and star anise, and serve at once.",
"Hand Pies|HF": "Fry bacon about 13 minutes and keep the fat. Cook potato about 7 minutes, then leeks, thyme, and garlic. Brown beef 4 to 5 minutes, stir in flour, broth, and salt, and thicken 2 minutes. Combine with bacon and parsley and cool 20 minutes. Fill pastry ovals, fold, seal, and vent. Brush with egg and bake at 375°F for 40 to 45 minutes.",
"Handsun and Halloumi Fritto Misto|HFLOTT": "Cut mango and halloumi into ½-inch batons. Whisk a thin batter of flour, cornstarch, baking powder, paprika, cayenne, salt, water, and oil, and chill 45 to 60 minutes. Heat 2 inches of oil to 375°F. Dip about 8 pieces at a time and fry 5 to 7 minutes until pale gold. Salt, keep warm at 200°F, and fry the halloumi last. Serve with lemon.",
"Hardbuckler Stew|HF": "Brown mushrooms about 20 minutes total and set aside. Preheat the oven to 325°F. Brown floured lamb in two batches, 3 to 4 minutes per side. Soften onion with thyme and bay leaves, add broth and lamb, cover, and bake 40 minutes. Add turnips for 30 minutes, then potatoes and mushrooms for about 1¼ hours. Finish with vinegar and parsley.",
"Harengon Coffee Carrots|HFFOTM": "Simmer carrots with espresso, molasses, and salt, covered, for 4 to 5 minutes until nearly tender. Add butter and thyme, then boil uncovered 4 to 5 minutes until the liquid reduces to about 3 tablespoons and the carrots are glazed. Off heat, stir in vinegar, vanilla, and pepper. Top with parsley and serve immediately.",
"Harmonious Barracks Meatloaf|HFFOTM": "Preheat the oven to 375°F. Soak bread in milk for 15 minutes, mash, and stir in eggs. Soften onion, then garlic, rosemary, and thyme, and cool. Fold in ground lamb, chuck, the onion mix, salt, pepper, and parsley. Shape a 9 by 5-inch loaf on a foil-lined rack. Bake about 1¼ hours until 155° to 160°F. Rest 10 minutes and slice.",
"Harpell's Reserve|PAF": "Boil cane sugar and water until dissolved, then cool. Put an oak infusion spiral in a swing-top bottle with bourbon, 2¼ ounces syrup, and bitters. Shake and store somewhere cool for 48 hours to 1 week, shaking daily. Pour 2½ ounces over a large ice cube per glass. Garnish with a Luxardo cherry and orange peel.",
"Heartlands Rose Apple and Blackberry Pie|HF": "Microwave sugared, spiced apples 7 to 10 minutes and cool 30 minutes. Line a deep-dish plate with pastry and chill 30 minutes. Preheat the oven to 425°F. Layer sugared blackberries with lemon juice, butter, and the apples. Cover with pastry, crimp, and egg-wash. Bake 25 minutes, then at 375°F for 25 to 30 minutes. Cool about 2 hours.",
"Hellish Rebuke|PAF": "Broil jalapeños 3 to 5 minutes per side until charred, peel, halve into spears, and steep in tequila for 1 to 3 hours. Shake 4 ounces of that tequila with orange liqueur, lime juice, and agave over ice for about 30 seconds. Strain into two ice-filled rocks glasses rimmed with chili-lime salt. Garnish with lime wheel and jalapeño slice.",
"High Harvest Puree|HF": "Preheat the oven to 425°F. Toss squash and garlic cloves with olive oil, salt, and pepper. Roast on a rimmed sheet about 30 minutes. Stir in thyme and roast 10 minutes more. Peel the garlic, return it to the squash, and mash to the desired texture. Drizzle with olive oil and serve.",
"High Sun Florentines|PAF": "Preheat the oven to 350°F. Boil sugar, cream, corn syrup, and butter for 1 minute, then add vanilla. Stir into ground almonds, flour, cocoa, orange zest, cayenne, and salt. Cool 20 minutes. Bake tablespoon balls, 3 to 4 inches apart, 10 to 11 minutes. Cut into rounds after 5 minutes. Drizzle with melted dark chocolate, add salt, chili flakes, and gold leaf. Chill 10 minutes.",
"Hogs in Bedrolls|HF": "Preheat the oven to 400°F. Cut puff pastry into 2-inch squares. Lay a cocktail frank diagonally on each, fold two corners over it, and pinch. Space 1 inch apart, brush with egg beaten with 1 tablespoon water, and bake about 17 minutes, rotating midway. Cool about 5 minutes. Serve hot with dipping sauces.",
"Holga's Potatoes|HFLOTT": "Microwave pricked potatoes 18 to 25 minutes until tender. Cut off the top third and scoop out the flesh. Brush the shells with butter and bake cut-side down at 450°F for about 22 minutes. Cook shallots, thyme, garlic, half-and-half, and cream cheese, then rice in the potato flesh with cheese, scallions, and parsley. Fill the shells, top with cheese, and bake 18 to 25 minutes.",
"Holiday Rib Roast|HFLOTT": "Salt the trimmed, scored roast and chill uncovered 24 to 72 hours. Rest 2 hours, then sear about 3 minutes per side. Make a stuffing of toasted bread, mushrooms, brandy, shallots, garlic, thyme, spinach, broth, and eggs. Pack it under the meat, tie, and roast at 275°F for about 2¼ hours to 120° to 125°F. Rest 10 minutes. Bake extra stuffing at 400°F for 25 minutes.",
"Hommlet Golden Brown Roasted Turkey with Sausage Stuffing and Drippings|HF": "Dry bread cubes at 250°F for 45 minutes. Butter and season turkey drumsticks and roast on vegetables at 400°F for 1 to 1¼ hours until 180° to 185°F. Bake a sausage, onion, celery, herb, broth, and egg stuffing covered for about 50 minutes. Make gravy from the drippings, bacon, and a flour roux. Broil the drumsticks 5 to 7 minutes and the stuffing 5 to 7 minutes.",
"Honey Milk|HFFOTM": "Heat milk and honey on medium to a bare simmer, stirring until the honey dissolves. Cool until barely warm. Pour into a sealed container and chill about 3 hours before serving.",
"Honey-Drizzled Cream Puffs|HF": "Preheat the oven to 425°F. Boil water, milk, butter, sugar, and salt, beat in flour, and cook 3 minutes. Process with eggs and vanilla into a sticky paste, then pipe 2-inch mounds. Bake 15 minutes, then at 375°F for 7 to 9 minutes. Slit and dry in the turned-off oven about 40 minutes. Fill with honeyed whipped cream and crème fraîche and drizzle with honey.",
"Honeyed Ham with Pineapple Gravy|HF": "Bring the ham to room temperature in 1½ to 2 hours. Wrap in foil and bake at 300°F for 3 to 3½ hours to about 120°F. Reduce pineapple juice to 1 cup for a honey, mustard, and clove glaze. Open the foil, glaze twice at 400°F, for 15 and then 8 minutes. Rest 15 minutes. Thicken a sauce of shallot, thyme, honey, mustard, ham juices, and pineapple with cornstarch.",
"Honeyflame Bread|HFLOTT": "Preheat the oven to 375°F. Rub butter into flours, baking soda, cream of tartar, and salt. Stir in buttermilk dissolved with honey. Knead briefly into a shaggy 6-inch round, put in a 10-inch cast-iron skillet, cut a deep cross, and brush with butter. Bake 40 to 45 minutes, rotating midway. Cool at least 30 minutes.",
"Hordelander|PAF": "Blend yogurt, vodka, lemon juice, mint, black pepper, and salt until smooth. Stir in soda water. Divide between two highball glasses half-filled with ice. Garnish each with a mint sprig and serve at once.",
"Hot River Crab Bites|HFFOTM": "Dry the crabmeat and remove any shell. Mix it with lemon juice, salt, pepper, crème fraîche, lemon zest, and most of the chives. Spoon about 1 tablespoon into each of sixteen endive leaves, sprinkle with the remaining chives, and serve immediately.",
"Hot Spiced Cider|HF": "Peel orange zest in strips and stud some with cloves. Toast allspice and cinnamon sticks 1 to 2 minutes, then add cider, cranberry juice, brown sugar, and clove zest. Simmer partially covered about 20 minutes and steep covered 20 minutes more. Strain, reheat to a simmer, and add vanilla. Serve in preheated mugs with zest and cranberries.",
"Illuskan Mulled Cider|PAF": "Combine apple cider, maple syrup, ginger, cinnamon sticks, cloves, allspice, cardamom, star anise, apple, orange, and half the hard cider. Bring to a bare simmer, then cook covered on low for 1 to 3 hours. Strain, stir in the rest of the hard cider, garnish with nutmeg, and serve at once.",
"Inkpot Negroni|PAF": "Muddle blackberries in a mixing glass. Add gin, Campari, amaro, and ice, and stir about 30 seconds. Put 1 to 2 large ice cubes in two glasses, strain the drink into them, and garnish each with a tarragon sprig and 3 blackberries. Serve at once.",
"Irlymeyer's Dragonfire Punch|HFFOTM": "Stir cranberry juice cocktail, orange and pineapple juice concentrates, lemon juice, and brandy in a pitcher. It keeps refrigerated 1 day. To serve, add ice, then gently stir in Prosecco. Pour over ice and garnish each glass with an orange slice.",
"Iron Rations|HF": "No cooking is needed. Divide the cheese, salami, dried fruit, nuts, crackers, and fresh fruit among four plates. For the trail, pack everything together or in four containers.",
"Jhuild|HFLOTT": "Keep 2 slices each of lemon and chile for garnish. Muddle the rest of the lemon and chile with ginger, turmeric, and sugar until syrupy. Add ice and rum and shake at least 15 seconds. Divide between two ice-filled old-fashioned glasses. Top each with 1½ ounces seltzer, stir gently, garnish with the reserved slices, and serve immediately.",
"Kaeth|HFFOTM": "Put ground coffee in a French press. Boil water with brown sugar, molasses, a cinnamon stick, anise seeds, orange zest, and salt, then simmer about 14 minutes until reduced to about 2⅔ cups. Pour over the coffee, stir, and steep 4 minutes. Press slowly and serve immediately.",
"Kale Soup with Sausage and Potatoes|HFLOTT": "Brown sausage in oil about 4 minutes and drain, saving the red oil. Soften onions with herbs about 8 minutes, then add garlic 40 seconds. Add broth and potatoes and cook about 9 minutes until soft. Thicken by mashing some potatoes if you like. Stir in sliced kale, tomatoes, and sausage and simmer about 4 minutes. Add salt, pepper, and vinegar. Drizzle with the saved oil.",
"Kara-Tur Noodles|HF": "Marinate chicken in soy sauce, rice wine, and sesame oil for 15 to 60 minutes. Soak noodles in boiling water about 6 minutes, rinse, and oil them. Brown the chicken in two batches, about 2 minutes each. Cook onion 2 to 3 minutes, then pepper and celery 2 to 3 minutes. Fry ginger and garlic 1 minute, thicken the sauce 1 minute, and toss all with the noodles 2 minutes.",
"Karrnathi Breaded Veal|HFLOTT": "Microwave bread about 5 minutes to dry it, then grind to fine crumbs. Pound four pork cutlets to ¼ inch, season, and rest 5 minutes. Dredge in flour, egg with oil, then crumbs, and dry on a rack 5 minutes. Fry two at a time in oil at 375°F, about 2 minutes per side. Blot, keep warm at 200°F, and serve with lemon.",
"Kender Loaf|HFFOTM": "Preheat the oven to 350°F. Hollow out a bread loaf, keeping the shell, and toast the torn pieces 20 to 25 minutes. Soak the pieces and raisins about 20 minutes in lemon sugar, half-and-half, eggs, yolks, vanilla, and salt. Butter the shell, add cinnamon sugar, fill, and top with more. Bake 35 to 40 minutes. Cool until warm and slice.",
"Kender Stumblenoodles|HFFOTM": "Preheat the oven to 375°F. Make a roux of butter, flour, paprika, garlic powder, and cayenne, whisk in milk, and simmer about 8 minutes. Melt in mustard, cream cheese, and Cheddar. Boil fusilli to 2 minutes short of al dente, toss with the sauce and Gruyère, and spread in a 13 by 9-inch dish. Top with buttered panko. Bake 30 to 40 minutes, then rest 8 to 10 minutes.",
"Kendermore Cobbler|HFFOTM": "Drain sugared peaches for 1 hour. Toss with blueberries, brown sugar, cornstarch, cloves, bourbon, and vanilla in an 8-inch pan. Preheat the oven to 425°F. Mix a buttermilk biscuit dough, shape nine rounds, dust with cinnamon sugar, and parbake about 7 minutes. Bake the filling 30 to 40 minutes, add the biscuits, and bake about 15 minutes more. Cool 25 minutes.",
"Kinship Shrub|PAF": "Mash lemon, rosemary, cumin seeds, and sugar in a jar and macerate 2 hours. Add vinegar and rest in a cool, dry place for 3 days, shaking daily. Strain. It keeps refrigerated for months. For each drink, pour 1¼ ounces shrub over ice and top with 4 ounces club soda. Garnish with lemon rounds and rosemary.",
"Krigala Supreme|HFLOTT": "Warm two glasses with boiling water for about 2 minutes, then empty them. Whisk cream about 45 seconds until thick but pourable. In each glass stir 1½ ounces bourbon, ½ ounce Frangelico, and 1½ teaspoons brown sugar, then add ¾ cup coffee. Float the cream over a spoon, dust with nutmeg, and serve immediately.",
"Lady Ophala|PAF": "Stir Campari and vermouth with ice for 30 seconds. Strain evenly into two coupe glasses. Add 2 ounces sparkling wine to each and stir gently. Top each with a scoop of vanilla ice cream.",
"Lamb Hocks with Apricot|HFLOTT": "Preheat the oven to 325°F. Brown four lamb shanks, about 9 minutes each. Soften onions with cinnamon, add garlic and spices for 45 seconds, then tomatoes and 1 cup water. Return the lamb, cover, and bake 90 minutes. Add carrots for 60 minutes, then apricots for about 30 minutes. Skim the sauce, add honey, lemon zest, and parsley, and reheat the lamb in it.",
"Lathander's Bounty|PAF": "Blend peaches, mango, yogurt, raspberries, and honey until smooth. Add 4 basil leaves and ice cubes and blend again. Stir in club soda. Divide between two highball glasses, garnish each with a basil leaf and edible flowers, and serve at once.",
"Laumberry Pie|HFFOTM": "Fit pastry into two 5-inch pie plates and freeze 30 minutes. Blind bake at 350°F for 25 to 30 minutes with weights, then about 12 minutes without. Cook a strained berry puree with sugar, cornstarch, and salt about 20 minutes until pudding-like, then add lemon juice and vanilla. Toss fresh berries in warm apple jelly. Fill the crusts and chill about 3 hours to 1 day.",
"Lemon Blueberry Trailcake|HFLOTT": "Preheat the oven to 450°F with a 10-inch cast-iron skillet inside. Blend eggs, milk, vanilla, lemon sugar, flour, and salt. Melt butter in the hot skillet and blend it in. Pour the batter into the pan, add floured blueberries, and bake 15 to 17 minutes until risen and browned. Squeeze lemon over it, dust with confectioners' sugar, cut, and serve at once.",
"Library Martini|PAF": "Infuse gin with chopped sage and lemon peel in a cool, dry place for 24 hours to 4 days, shaking daily, then strain. Stir 4 ounces of that gin with vermouth and ice for about 30 seconds. Strain evenly into martini glasses, top each with a sage leaf, and serve at once.",
"Littlewinter|PAF": "Boil the water, then remove from heat and stir in brandy, red vermouth, maple syrup, and lemon juice. Put 1 cinnamon stick and 3 pear slices in each heatproof mug. Ladle in the punch and serve at once.",
"Lluirwood Salad|HF": "Whisk a vinaigrette of vinegar, lemon juice, mustard, shallot, salt, pepper, and olive oil in a salad bowl. Reserve 1½ tablespoons. Toss spinach in the rest, then add salt, pepper, goat cheese, and most of the nuts and cranberries. Top with the remaining nuts and cranberries and the reserved dressing.",
"Loaf Pudding|HFFOTM": "Preheat the oven to 350°F. Cream butter and sugar about 3 minutes, beat in eggs, vanilla, and almond extract, then alternate flour, almond meal, and yogurt. Top with sliced almonds and bake about 45 minutes. Cool 8 minutes in the pan. Simmer sugar syrup about 6 minutes, cool, and flavor. Poke the warm loaf and brush it with syrup. Keeps 2 days.",
"Loklee|PAF": "Stir bourbon, sweet vermouth, amaro, balsamic vinegar, and bitters with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain evenly into two cocktail glasses. Garnish with orange peel and serve at once.",
"Luiric Rarebit|PAF": "Broil on high with the rack 6 inches from the element. Brown butter and flour 2 to 3 minutes, then add mustard, cayenne, Worcestershire, and dark ale. On low, melt in three-quarters of the cheese. Toast bread about 2 minutes, flip, top with the cheese sauce and remaining cheese, and broil 3 to 5 minutes until bubbling. Halve and top with chives.",
"Madame Rosene's Nightcap|PAF": "Stir brandy, amaro, vermouth, and bitters with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain evenly into two coupe glasses and serve at once.",
"Magic Jar|PAF": "Combine gin, falernum, pineapple juice, carrot juice, and lemon juice in a punch bowl. Add large ice cubes to half fill, top with ginger beer, and stir gently. Ladle into six jars half-filled with crushed ice. Top with cucumber, mint, strawberries, kiwi, starfruit, edible flowers, or a chili-lime salt rim.",
"Magister's Delight|HFLOTT": "Preheat the oven to 350°F. Cream butter and sugar about 3 minutes, beat in eggs, then alternate the spiced flour mix with eggnog, rum, and vanilla. Bake in a greased 10-inch Bundt pan 45 to 55 minutes, rotating midway. Cool 10 minutes, turn out, and cool fully. Drizzle with a rum, nutmeg, and cinnamon glaze and set about 20 minutes.",
"Malatran Mule|PAF": "Simmer water, sugar, and lemongrass covered for 10 minutes, steep 30 to 60 minutes, strain, and cool. In each highball glass, bruise a chile if using, 4 basil leaves, 4 mint leaves, 5 cilantro leaves, and half the lime juice. Fill with ice, add 2 ounces vodka and ¼ ounce syrup, top with ginger beer, and stir gently.",
"Many Stars|PAF": "Simmer water, sugar, a cinnamon stick, clove, and star anise for 5 minutes, then cool. In a pitcher, stir pear, orange, pomegranate arils, ¼ cup syrup, and the spices. Add red wine, fruit juices, brandy, and orange liqueur. Chill at least 4 hours, ideally overnight. Serve over ice with fruit and a rosemary sprig.",
"Meal's End|HF": "Chop 2 cups of strawberries and slice 1 cup, sweetening each to taste. Whip cream to soft peaks, adding 1 tablespoon sugar once it thickens, 1 to 1½ minutes in a stand mixer. Fold in yogurt, vanilla, chopped berries, and crumbled meringues. Divide among four dishes, top with the sliced berries, and serve at once.",
"Melted Cheeses with Chunky Tomato Broth|HF": "Soften onion in butter about 5 minutes, add brown sugar and tomato paste for 1 minute, then broth, rice, and most of the tomatoes. Simmer covered about 20 minutes, puree, and stir in the chopped reserved tomatoes. Butter eight bread slices, fill four sandwiches with grated cheese, and griddle 3 to 5 minutes per side. Cut into strips and serve with the soup and herbs.",
"Midnight Mushroom Caps|HFLOTT": "Preheat the oven to 425°F. Toss caps in oil, lemon juice, and salt and roast gill-side up about 15 minutes. Drain, flip, and roast 6 to 10 minutes. Brown halloumi 2 to 3 minutes per side and crumble. Cook chopped stems 7 minutes, then shallots, thyme, garlic, and zest 3 minutes. Mix with halloumi, pine nuts, parsley, and ricotta. Fill the caps and roast 15 to 18 minutes.",
"Miner's Pie|HF": "Soften onion and leek about 4 minutes, brown beef about 10 minutes, then add garlic, thyme, tomato paste, flour, ale, and broth. Simmer about 15 minutes, add corn and peas, and put in a casserole. Steam potatoes about 20 minutes, rice with butter, milk, and Parmesan, cool 20 minutes, and add eggs. Top with potatoes and Monterey Jack. Bake at 450°F 20 minutes, broil 5 to 7.",
"Mingari-Spiced Owlbear Milk|HFFOTM": "Toast oatmeal 4 to 5 minutes, add water, milk, both sugars, salt, and cinnamon sticks. Simmer about 7 minutes, then on low about 5 minutes. Cool, chill 4 to 24 hours, blend, and strain. Chill the strained milk with the sticks about 1 hour. Shake, thin with up to ¾ cup milk if needed, and pour over ice if desired. Dust with cinnamon.",
"Mintarn Almond Brandy|HFLOTT": "Fill two glasses a third full of ice. Divide brandy, amaretto, and lemon juice between them and stir gently. Express a lemon twist over each glass, run it around the rim, drop it in, and serve immediately.",
"Minted Pea Soup|HFLOTT": "Soften red onion in a vinegar, water, sugar, and salt pickle for 30 minutes. Soften leek in butter about 6 minutes, stir in flour for 1 minute, then add 3 cups broth. Add peas, boil, and simmer covered about 3 minutes. Add 1 cup broth and 1 cup water, blend with mint, and strain. Reheat with half-and-half. Top with mint, Boursin, and the pickled onion.",
"Mintwater|PAF": "Blend 2 cups water, sugar, and lime juice for 30 seconds. Add cucumbers and mint and blend smooth. Strain into a pitcher and stir in 2 more cups water. Serve over ice in rocks glasses with extra mint leaves.",
"Moonrise|PAF": "Muddle blackberries, stir in lemonade, and strain. Fill two highball glasses three-quarters with ice. Stir grenadine with black food coloring and divide it between the glasses. Slowly layer half the coconut cream liqueur, then half the blackberry lemonade, in each. Top each with 2 ounces tequila and 2 blackberries. Serve at once.",
"Moonshae Seafood Rice|HF": "Keep stock warm and steep saffron in ½ cup of it. Soften onion about 4 minutes, toast rice 2 to 3 minutes, and absorb the wine about 2 minutes. Add 1 cup stock at a time, three times, about 5 minutes each. Add shrimp and scallops for 2 minutes, then the saffron stock for about 3 minutes until creamy and al dente. Stir in butter and serve with chives.",
"Morning Cookies|HFLOTT": "Preheat the oven to 350°F. Process oats, prunes, and sesame seeds. Process butter and brown sugar, then add eggs with maple syrup, vanilla, and sesame oil, the flour mix, and the oats for about 45 seconds. Pat into a lined 13 by 9-inch pan and bake 30 to 35 minutes, rotating. Cool 20 minutes, lift out, trim, and cut 3-inch crescents. Keeps 5 days.",
"Mother|PAF": "Stir together tomato juice, horseradish, Worcestershire, hot sauce, lemon juice, caper brine, oyster water, fish sauce if using, salt, celery salt, and pepper. The mix keeps 1 week refrigerated. Put 4 ounces of mix and 2 ounces vodka over ice in each of two highball glasses, stir, and garnish with an oyster. Serve at once.",
"Mourning Cup|PAF": "Bruise rosemary, add tea bags, and cover with a boiled mix of ½ cup water and honey. After 30 seconds, pour it all into a carafe holding 2½ cups cold water. Steep refrigerated 4 to 8 hours. Strain, add rose water if using, and serve over ice in two highball glasses.",
"Mushroom Tea|HF": "Soak kombu in water for 30 minutes, then heat 10 to 12 minutes to a simmer and discard the kombu. Boil about 3 minutes, add shiitakes, soy sauce, and salt, and cook 1 to 2 minutes until tender. Stir in sake. Serve topped with scallions.",
"Necromancer|PAF": "Rinse two chilled coupe glasses with ¼ ounce absinthe each and discard the excess. Shake gin, orange liqueur, fortified red wine, lemon juice, and blood orange juice with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain evenly into the glasses, garnish with blood orange wheels, and serve at once.",
"Nether Gold|PAF": "Boil water and honey, add a tea bag, steep 10 minutes, and cool. Muddle ginger in a shaker, then add blended scotch, lemon juice, 1½ ounces chamomile honey syrup, and bitters, plus ice. Shake about 30 seconds. Strain over large cubes in two glasses. Float ¼ ounce peated scotch on each over a spoon. Serve at once.",
"Neverwinter Nectar|HFFOTM": "Slice an orange and a lemon, mix with sugar for 20 minutes, then muddle until syrupy. Add apple juice, brandy, and wine and chill 4 to 24 hours. Strain, pressing the solids. Add thin slices of a second orange and an apple to the pitcher, then seltzer and ice. Serve over ice.",
"Night Watch|PAF": "Stir vodka, coffee liqueur, cold brew concentrate, Licor 43, and orange juice with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain evenly over ice into two rocks glasses. Garnish with orange peel and serve at once.",
"Noble Pretender|PAF": "Muddle peaches and strawberries in a shaker. Add amaretto, cranberry juice, lemon juice, and ice. Shake 30 seconds. Strain evenly over ice into two rocks glasses and serve at once.",
"Ogre Mutton Stew|HFLOTT": "Preheat the oven to 325°F. Brown floured lamb in three batches, about 3½ minutes per side. Soften onions, chopped carrots, thyme, and bay leaves about 6 minutes, add broth and lamb, cover, and bake 1 hour. Add carrot chunks and potatoes and bake about 1¼ hours more until tender. Mash some potatoes to thicken if wanted. Finish with parsley.",
"Ogretoe|PAF": "Shake whiskey, vermouth, pickle juice, and lemon juice with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain evenly over ice into two rocks glasses. Garnish with dill and pickles and serve at once.",
"Onion Loaf|HFFOTM": "Preheat the oven to 375°F. Cook onion about 3 minutes and leek about 3 minutes in butter and oil, then cool. Mix a dough of flours, onion powder, baking powder, baking soda, salt, eggs, brown sugar, buttermilk, melted butter, and scallions. Shape an 8-inch log in a buttered dish and press the onions on top. Bake 45 to 50 minutes, rotating. Cool 10 minutes in the dish.",
"Orange Mountain Duck|HF": "Zest and segment oranges and keep ⅔ cup juice. Preheat the oven to 200°F. Score duck breasts and cook skin-side down on medium 12 to 14 minutes, then flip until 125°F for medium-rare or 130° to 135°F for medium, 2 to 8 minutes. Rest 5 minutes in the oven. Reduce shallot, thyme, juice, and broth, then add honey, brandy, cayenne, zest, and butter. Slice the duck over the sauce.",
"Ornabra|HFFOTM": "Preheat the oven to 325°F. Brown floured lamb in batches, about 3½ minutes per side. Cook finely chopped carrots, onions, bay leaves, and rosemary about 10 minutes, then tomato paste about 1½ minutes. Add broth and lamb, cover, and bake 1½ hours. Add carrot chunks and potatoes and bake 40 to 60 minutes more. Finish with vinegar and parsley.",
"Otik's Skillet-Fried Spiced Potatoes|HF": "Cook onion in oil about 8 to 10 minutes until deep golden and set aside. Microwave potatoes 5 to 7 minutes. Fry them in oil and butter over medium-high heat without stirring, 6 to 7 minutes, then about 6 minutes on the next side. Keep turning 6 to 12 minutes more until browned. Season with salt, pepper, paprika, cayenne, and garlic powder, return the onion, and top with chives.",
}
